^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}={e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-2{e}^{2x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}({z}^{2}+2{e}^{x}z+{e}^{2x})-2{e}^{2x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{3x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331609 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331610 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331611 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331612 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331613 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1041 "selection" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331612 13194139535107 true] [17592186331608 1110 #uuid "63ea368c-104c-504b-b184-cd6f46cc7992" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331609 1034 "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331609 1111 #uuid "d126ec62-6504-5cd6-94c1-4c823bd7a85a" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331610 1034 "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}-C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331610 1111 #uuid "9c354376-6b55-582f-87db-f713f7f9e5b7" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331611 1034 "y={e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331611 1111 #uuid "d71af105-5ce1-5757-80d5-8ed5bd63c67d" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331612 1034 "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331612 1111 #uuid "9b664bf2-8764-589f-a443-6e8a7d17f594" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331613 1034 "y={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{x}+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331613 1111 #uuid "e402141c-6190-5bd8-b1cb-7dd37debd2e0" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331615 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1089 "q-334096" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1100 "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=x+1$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}-6(x+1)y+3{x}^{2}+6x+4\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1113 #uuid "ec40b5fc-8430-5d44-8beb-1e0c0c65c606" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331614 1145 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}-6(x+1)y+3{x}^{2}+6x+4,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=3,\\,b(x)=-6(x+1),\\,c(x)=3{x}^{2}+6x+4.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=x+1.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+x+1\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+1=3(z+x+1)^{2}-6(x+1)(z+x+1)+3{x}^{2}+6x+4.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+1 & =3((x+1)^{2}+2(x+1)z+{z}^{2})-6(x+1)(z+x+1)+3{x}^{2}+6x+4 \\\\ {z}^{′}+1 & =3{z}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =3x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-(x+1)$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y-(x+1) & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}+x+1 \\\\  & =x+1-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331616 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331617 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331618 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331619 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331620 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1041 "selection" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331620 13194139535107 true] [17592186331615 1110 #uuid "0646cb5c-b420-58ba-b062-5b5048bffc35" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331616 1034 "y=x+1-\\frac{1}{x+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331616 1111 #uuid "04333c63-2e58-5790-bbc9-6d950fdedbcd" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331617 1034 "y=x+1+\\frac{2}{3x-C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331617 1111 #uuid "933a72ae-2a44-586c-a6cd-a8a6b5e6f7b7" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331618 1034 "y=x+1+\\frac{2}{3x+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331618 1111 #uuid "dbc84afc-2228-5d51-8e4f-6ba1fb8b790e" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331619 1034 "y=x+1+\\frac{1}{3x+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331619 1111 #uuid "56c2bee2-34db-5d8d-94b5-d2e1238a2d9d" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331620 1034 "y=x+1-\\frac{1}{3x+C}" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535107 true] [17592186331620 1111 #uuid "5c4cdcd4-7d8d-5486-aaff-c9656ecadcba" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331622 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1089 "q-334122" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1100 "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,y+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1113 #uuid "cfdc15b3-f049-5c54-b917-bb040b11bf90" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331621 1145 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,y+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=2x,\\,b(x)=-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,c(x)=2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=2x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2x({z}^{2}+2z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,(z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+2x{cos}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {z}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2x{z}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535107 true] [17592186331622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331623 13194